description: Rules for dealing with Next.js App Router pages and components
alwaysApply: false
---
You are an expert in Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript, and TailwindCSS for scalable web development.

Key Principles
- Write concise, technical responses with accurate Next.js App Router examples
- Use Server Components by default, only use Client Components when necessary
- Leverage React Server Components for optimal performance
- Use TypeScript for type safety across all components
- Follow shadcn/ui component patterns and best practices

Project Structure
- next-app/
    - app/
        - actions/      # Server Actions (marked with 'use server')
        - [routes]/     # App Router pages
        - layout.tsx     # Root layout
    - components/
        - ui/          # shadcn/ui components
    - lib/            # utility functions, PocketBase helpers, type definitions
    - public/         # static assets
    - next.config.mjs # Next.js configuration
    - tsconfig.json   # TypeScript configuration

Component Development
- Server Components are the default - use them unless you need interactivity
- Use `'use client'` directive only when you need:
  - React hooks (useState, useEffect, etc.)
  - Event handlers (onClick, onChange, etc.)
  - Browser APIs (window, localStorage, etc.)
  - Third-party libraries that require client-side execution
- Follow common React component patterns (see [react-components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/react-components.mdc))
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Keep components simple and focused on UI concerns
- Use shadcn/ui components as the foundation for UI elements
- Import types from `@/lib/definitions` for shared data types (see [data-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/data-types.mdc))

Styling Guidelines
- **See [nextjs-styling.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/nextjs-styling.mdc) for comprehensive styling rules**
- Use TailwindCSS v4 exclusively for styling - ALL styles must go through Tailwind utility classes
- Never use inline `style` attributes, custom CSS files, or CSS modules
- **CRITICAL**: Use semantic color names (primary, secondary, accent, destructive, muted, etc.) instead of explicit colors (red, green, blue, etc.)
- Never use explicit Tailwind color names like `bg-red-500`, `text-blue-600` - use `bg-primary`, `text-accent-foreground` instead
- Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- Configuration is done via Tailwind CSS v4 (tailwind.config.ts for content paths)

Server Actions
- Server Actions are defined in `next-app/app/actions/` directory
- Mark server actions with `'use server'` directive at the top of the file
- Actions accept `FormData` or other parameters and return state objects
- Use `useActionState` hook in Client Components to handle form state
- Validate input with Zod schemas before processing
- Handle errors gracefully and return error states in the response
- Use `redirect()` from `next/navigation` for navigation after actions
- Handle redirect errors by checking for `NEXT_REDIRECT` digest

Data Fetching
- Server-side: Use direct database calls or API calls in Server Components
- Use `async/await` in Server Components for data fetching
- Client-side: Use React hooks (useState, useEffect) or Server Actions from Client Components
- Use PocketBase client from `@/lib/pocketbase-server` for database operations
- Access cookies via `cookies()` from `next/headers` in Server Components/Actions

Authentication
- Use `getAuthenticatedUser()` from `@/lib/pocketbase-server` to check auth status
- Redirect unauthenticated users using `redirect()` from `next/navigation`
- Store auth tokens in HTTP-only cookies via `cookies().set()`
- Initialize PocketBase with `initPocketBase()` to load auth from cookies
- Use `createPocketBase()` for new PocketBase instances in server actions

TypeScript Best Practices
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Define interfaces for all props and data structures
- Use Zod schemas in `next-app/lib/definitions.ts` for runtime validation
- Import types using `type` keyword when importing only types
- Use `@/` alias for imports (configured in tsconfig.json)

Server Component Guidelines
- Server Components are async by default
- Can directly access filesystem, databases, and environment variables
- Cannot use browser APIs or React hooks
- Can pass Server Components as children to Client Components

Client Component Guidelines
- Must be marked with `'use client'` directive
- Can use React hooks and browser APIs
- Use `useActionState` for form handling with Server Actions
- Keep Client Components small and focused on interactivity

Code Quality
- Keep components modular and reusable
- Document complex logic with clear comments
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Follow existing code patterns in the codebase
- Handle errors gracefully with proper error messages

Refer to Next.js 16 official documentation and shadcn/ui documentation for detailed component implementation guidelines.
